Spec: Retrail

Platform: Flutter/Dart/Material 3/Riverpod/Drift/MapLibre

Purpose:
  GPS route tracker for longboard, skate and other rolling-sport rides on Android and iOS,
    migrated from an Android Jetpack Compose app. Records rides offline, keeps a history with
    pre-rendered map previews, and lets a rider follow a saved route again.

Structure:
  ./lib: Flutter app code
  ./test: Unit, widget, provider, DAO, golden and scenario tests
  ./integration_test: On-device integration tests
  ./android: Android host app, service notification, platform channels, release signing
  ./ios: iOS host app, Live Activity extension, platform channels
  ./assets: Map styles, app icon and activity icons
  ./tool: Build, release, map-style and store-graphics scripts
  ./site: GitHub Pages site with privacy policy and imprint
  ./store: Play Store listing texts, screenshots and graphics
  ./docs: Release, store and sideloading guides; decision notes; spec history

Owns:
  ./pubspec.yaml
  ./pubspec.lock
  ./analysis_options.yaml
  ./l10n.yaml
  ./README.md
  ./LICENSE
  ./AGENTS.md
  ./CLAUDE.md
  ./.gitignore
  ./.git-blame-ignore-revs
  ./.githooks/pre-commit
  ./.githooks/pre-push
  ./.github/workflows/ios-build.yml
  ./.github/workflows/pages.yml
  ./integration_test
  ./docs

References:
  /docs/specs/history/01-foundation.md
  /docs/specs/history/15-polish-release.md

Must:
  Every behaviour of the original Android app is kept: distances, speeds, filters, formatting,
    GPS filtering thresholds and offline handling.
  App ID is `io.github.valijuu.retrail` on Android and iOS; debug builds add `.debug` and are
    labelled `Retrail Debug`.
  The repository stays public with all rights reserved.
  `main` stays green and linear.

Must not:
  Commit real ride or GPS data; real traces stay in gitignored fixtures.
  Commit release bundles, signing keys or `android/key.properties`.

Done when:
  `flutter analyze` is clean.
  `flutter test` passes.
  Every changed Dart file is formatted with `dart format`.
